<title>JAPAN: NCB says to announce buyers of its new shares.</title>
<headline>NCB says to announce buyers of its new shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Credit Bank Ltd said on Thursday that the bank will announce the names of the buyers of its new shares at 4 p.m. (0700 GMT).</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the bank said that its board formally approved a plan to issue 766.04 million new shares, worth 167 billion yen, in a third-party allotment.</p>
<p>The new shares, to be priced at 218 yen each, will be allocated to other banks and life and non-life insurance companies, NCB said at that time, adding that those firms had informally agreed to hold the new NCB shares for two years from the issuance.</p>
</text>
